{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03202",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.25,
      "end_seconds": 6.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "Hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.25,
      "end_seconds": 12.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.51,
      "end_seconds": 25.99,
      "duration_seconds": 12.48,
      "text": "Mainly a high temperature. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.89,
      "end_seconds": 31.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.83,
      "end_seconds": 44.61,
      "duration_seconds": 11.78,
      "text": "Ah, honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, I really can't pin it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.74,
      "end_seconds": 49.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.14,
      "end_seconds": 58.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "It feels mild to me. I've also been feeling very weak, for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.66,
      "end_seconds": 62.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.68,
      "end_seconds": 70.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "About a six out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.85,
      "end_seconds": 77.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Have you had a high temperature before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.39,
      "end_seconds": 84.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "A bit, about six months ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.94,
      "end_seconds": 103.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Have you had any rash, diarrhoea or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.88,
      "end_seconds": 118.78,
      "duration_seconds": 10.9,
      "text": "No, no rash, no diarrhoea, no cough. I did have a sore mouth at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.49,
      "end_seconds": 122.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.64,
      "end_seconds": 128.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.5,
      "end_seconds": 132.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.79,
      "end_seconds": 135.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.61,
      "end_seconds": 140.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.47,
      "end_seconds": 144.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "No, I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.54,
      "end_seconds": 150.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.74,
      "end_seconds": 157.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "Acid reflux, for five years. Yeah, I've had depression, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.27,
      "end_seconds": 168.84,
      "duration_seconds": 9.57,
      "text": "Right, so acid reflux is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.8,
      "end_seconds": 178.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Just a bunion operation, six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.54,
      "end_seconds": 183.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.64,
      "end_seconds": 192.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a round yellow one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.59,
      "end_seconds": 196.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.62,
      "end_seconds": 224.24,
      "duration_seconds": 26.62,
      "text": "For my acidity, I believe. My son sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Mirtazapine, 15 milligrams, at night for my mood. I do miss it now and then, to be fair. Chemotherapy last week, recent. I, I had sertraline at one point, but I'm off it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.09,
      "end_seconds": 227.04,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.84,
      "end_seconds": 232.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "I quit smoking around ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.24,
      "end_seconds": 236.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.12,
      "end_seconds": 242.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.72,
      "end_seconds": 246.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.68,
      "end_seconds": 250.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.48,
      "end_seconds": 253.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.2,
      "end_seconds": 258.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 259.46,
      "end_seconds": 267.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Heart rate 98, blood pressure 103 over 63, temperature 37.2, respiratory rate 19."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.01,
      "end_seconds": 269.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.41,
      "end_seconds": 275.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Alright, could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.54,
      "end_seconds": 279.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "So, tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.24,
      "end_seconds": 301.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "You are hot, shaking and your blood pressure is low, and you had chemotherapy nine days ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.78,
      "end_seconds": 305.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "All finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.39,
      "end_seconds": 326.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, this looks most like neutropenic sepsis. Another possibility is a chest infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.38,
      "end_seconds": 331.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "I mean, is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.85,
      "end_seconds": 348.05,
      "duration_seconds": 16.2,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's neutropenic sepsis, and we'll know more once the urgent blood tests is back. So, to recap quickly. You've had a high temperature, mild, and no cough or diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.02,
      "end_seconds": 350.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Mm, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.16,
      "end_seconds": 356.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "I want urgent blood tests done, that's for neutropenic sepsis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 357.72,
      "end_seconds": 362.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "We have a slot Friday at 3:30 pm, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.32,
      "end_seconds": 375.19,
      "duration_seconds": 11.87,
      "text": "You'll be taking piperacillin and tazobactam, 4.5 grams, now, single dose. That should help with neutropenic sepsis. This is an emergency, antibiotics are being given within the hour."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.61,
      "end_seconds": 389.3,
      "duration_seconds": 13.69,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.87,
      "end_seconds": 390.78,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.27,
      "end_seconds": 399.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "Let's review you straight away. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 401.49,
      "end_seconds": 403.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.91,
      "end_seconds": 406.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}